text: >-
  4

  Drone Spy Plane N1098L

  Spy Plane N1098L @ Sept 10th. Designed to drop off/pick up drones.

  AXEL10. HADES Spy program.

  The Flight N1098L is designed to launch military drones.

  Normally flies at 41,000' altitude. Dropped to 203' altitude

  116 knots stall speed @ 9:16am MT 1-mile from UVU.

  Then looped back to 1-mile from UVU and 203' altitude @

  stall speed 25 minutes after assassination.

  U.S. Army to Test Launching Drones

  from Aircraft

  by Julia Alexandrova - 11/01/2025 in Aviation news

  Army Wants To Test Air-Launched

  Drones From A Global Express

  Business Jet

  The planned trials tally with previous comments about launching the drones
  from the

  new Global 6500-based HADES surveillance jet.

  THOMAS NEWCK /PUGLISHED AN 2. 2265 433 PHEST SO 30

  24001

  n000

  3

  48

  SHARES

  VIEWS

  If

  X

  in

  The U.S. Army is considering testing drone launches from a specialized version
  of the Bombardier Global

  6500, designed for special missions. This initiative aims to enhance the
  capabilities of the service's High

  Accuracy Detection and Exploitation System (HADES), which is based on the
  Global 6500 platform. The

  first HADES aircraft was delivered in November last year. Concerns have long
  been raised about the

  survivability of HADES in contested airspaces, and integrating drone-launching
  capabilities is seen as

  potential way to address this challenge.
